705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278706 13194139534147 true] [17592186278705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534147 true] [17592186278705 1041 "field-1" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278706 13194139534147 true] [17592186278705 1110 #uuid "3f24f6f2-3176-56f2-8b27-3e5c708287b1" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278706 1034 "0" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278706 1111 #uuid "c1d49740-85d7-58b9-a984-3d2ff93cddf5" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278707 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278708 13194139534147 true] [17592186278707 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534147 true] [17592186278707 1041 "field-2" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278707 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278708 13194139534147 true] [17592186278707 1110 #uuid "7a90a74a-f436-5416-953e-1108052f80f8" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278708 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278708 1111 #uuid "53fcda15-4075-5c59-a89e-6810b3779231" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278710 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278712 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278714 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1089 "q-328528" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1100 "From **top to bottom**, the ellipse $\\frac{(x-8)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis at the points $A$ and $B.$ Find the coordinates of these points.\n\n$A($\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\frac{4}{5})\\,$\n\nand \n\n$\\,B($\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$)$" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1113 #uuid "5cf3595a-3dd1-5635-8b87-e3ce4b4ff3e4" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278709 1145 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-8)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-8)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{64}{100}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ 144+25(y+1)^{2} & =225 \\\\ 25(y+1)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =\\frac{81}{25} \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ y & =-1\\pm \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{14}{5},\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are\n\n$$\nA(0,\\frac{4}{5})\\,\\text{and}\\,B(0,-\\frac{14}{5}).\n$$" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278711 13194139534147 true] [17592186278710 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534147 true] [17592186278710 1041 "field-1" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278710 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278711 13194139534147 true] [17592186278710 1110 #uuid "bf59b56a-2201-57ba-a17d-debecf47d75a" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278711 1034 "0" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278711 1111 #uuid "a7c57d73-211f-5f9b-a24b-fecfdb7d9dec" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278713 13194139534147 true] [17592186278712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534147 true] [17592186278712 1041 "field-2" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278713 13194139534147 true] [17592186278712 1110 #uuid "9ccbcf92-e738-523a-a089-5d0d6a3d4ec6" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278713 1034 "0" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278713 1111 #uuid "780e62ad-1dca-5796-8f1f-810deffc292f" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278715 13194139534147 true] [17592186278714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534147 true] [17592186278714 1041 "field-3" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278715 13194139534147 true] [17592186278714 1110 #uuid "fa30dc44-6a4e-50f3-99eb-40f86b2c59c2" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278715 1034 "-\\frac{14}{5}" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278715 1111 #uuid "a056d34a-5cc0-5334-a095-adcabdd8afe2" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278717 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1089 "q-70184" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1100 "Calculate the points where the ellipse ${x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+4x+54y+76=0$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1113 #uuid "59316311-32d9-5b38-a573-15e21c936803" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278716 1145 "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+4x+54y+76 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9\\cdot {0}^{2}+4x+54\\cdot 0+76 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4x+76 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}-4+76 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+72 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x+2)^{2}\\ge 0$, there is no $x$ such that $(x+2)^{2}=-72.$ Therefore, the ellipse has no $x$-intercepts, meaning that it does not intercept the $x$-axis at any point." 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278718 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278719 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278720 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278721 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278722 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1041 "selection" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278719 13194139534147 true] [17592186278717 1110 #uuid "94db5a3c-1a9f-515d-968e-4116203c1941" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278718 1034 "(\\pm 6\\sqrt{2},0)" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534147 true] [17592186278718 1111 #uuid "4c05d5af-db75-591a-9db9-5fb2c5146301" 13194139534147 true] [17592186278719 1034 "Th